{"id":"eabe959f144d0a191d3402c0b8ec35eac6bf55e2","axis":"silent","repo":"payloadcms/payload","sha":"eabe959f144d0a191d3402c0b8ec35eac6bf55e2","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/queries/overview.mdx","lines":["@@ -41,14 +41,14 @@ The following operators are available for use in queries:"," "," | Operator             | Description                                                                                                                                                                      |"," | -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","-| `equals`             | The value must be exactly equal.                                                                                                                                                 |","-| `not_equals`         | The query will return all documents where the value is not equal.                                                                                                                |","+| `equals`             | The value must be exactly equal. With a nested query on a non-polymorphic `hasMany` relationship, every related document must match.                                             |","+| `not_equals`         | The query will return all documents where the value is not equal. With a nested query on a non-polymorphic `hasMany` relationship, no related document may match.                |"," | `greater_than`       | For numeric or date-based fields.                                                                                                                                                |"," | `greater_than_equal` | For numeric or date-based fields.                                                                                                                                                |"," | `less_than`          | For numeric or date-based fields.                                                                                                                                                |"," | `less_than_equal`    | For numeric or date-based fields.                                                                                                                                                |"," | `like`               | Case-insensitive string must be present. If string of words, all words must be present, in any order.                                                                            |","-| `contains`           | Must contain the value entered, case-insensitive.                                                                                                                                |","+| `contains`           | Must contain the value entered, case-insensitive. With a nested query on a non-polymorphic `hasMany` relationship, at least one related document must match.                     |"," | `in`                 | The value must be found within the provided comma-delimited list of values.                                                                                                      |"," | `not_in`             | The value must NOT be within the provided comma-delimited list of values.                                                                                                        |"," | `all`                | The value must contain all values provided in the comma-delimited list. Note: currently this operator is supported only with the MongoDB adapter.                                |","@@ -101,21 +101,109 @@ const query: Where = {"," "," Written in plain English, if the above query were passed to a `find` operation, it would translate to finding posts where either the `color` is `mint` OR the `color` is `white` AND `featured` is set to false."," ","-### Nested properties","+## Relationship queries"," ","-When working with nested properties, which can happen when using relational fields, it is possible to use the dot notation to access the nested property. For example, when working with a `Song` collection that has an `artists` field which is related to an `Artists` collection using the `name: 'artists'`. You can access a property within the collection `Artists` like so:","+Relationship fields can be queried through properties on their related documents. You can also","+apply a nested query to a non-polymorphic `hasMany` relationship or upload field."," ","-```js","+### Nested relationship properties","+","+Use dot notation to query a field on a related document. For example, if a `Song` collection has an","+`artists` relationship field, you can query the `featured` field from the related `Artists`","+collection like this:","+","+```ts"," import type { Where } from 'payload'"," "," const query: Where = {","+  // `featured` is the nested property name to filter on","   'artists.featured': {","-    // nested property name to filter on","-    exists: true, // operator to use and boolean value that needs to be true","+    exists: true,","   },"," }"," ```"," ","+For a `hasMany` relationship, a dot-notation query matches when at least one related document","+matches. For example, `'ingredients.isHealthy': { not_equals: false }` matches a burger when at","+least one ingredient has an `isHealthy` value other than `false`. A burger with healthy lettuce and","+an unhealthy sauce still matches because of the lettuce. Use the nested relationship operators","+below when you need to control how many related documents must match.","+","+### Has-many relationship operators","+","+For non-polymorphic `hasMany` relationship and upload fields, pass a nested query to `contains`,","+`not_equals`, or `equals` to control how many related documents must match. These examples assume","+that `burgers.ingredients` is a `hasMany` relationship and that each ingredient has an `isHealthy`","+field:","+","+```ts","+import type { Where } from 'payload'","+","+// At least one ingredient is healthy.","+const hasHealthyIngredient: Where = {","+  ingredients: {","+    contains: {","+      isHealthy: { equals: true },","+    },","+  },","+}","+","+// No ingredient is unhealthy.","+const hasNoUnhealthyIngredient: Where = {","+  ingredients: {","+    not_equals: {","+      isHealthy: { equals: false },","+    },","+  },","+}","+","+// Every ingredient is healthy.","+const hasOnlyHealthyIngredients: Where = {","+  ingredients: {","+    equals: {","+      isHealthy: { equals: true },","+    },","+  },","+}","+```","+","+| Operator     | Description                                                |","+| ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- |","+| `contains`   | At least one related document must match the nested query. |","+| `not_equals` | No related document may match the nested query.            |","+| `equals`     | Every related document must match the nested query.        |","+","+The value passed to the relationship operator is a normal Payload `where` query. It supports field","+operators, deeper relationship queries, and the same `and` and `or` groups as any other Payload","+query. All conditions inside one operator are evaluated against the same related document:","+","+```ts","+const burgers = await payload.find({","+  collection: 'burgers',","+  where: {","+    ingredients: {","+      contains: {","+        and: [","+          { isHealthy: { equals: true } },","+          {","+            or: [","+              { name: { equals: 'lettuce' } },","+              { name: { equals: 'tomato' } },","+            ],","+          },","+        ],","+      },","+    },","+  },","+})","+```","+","+This finds burgers with at least one healthy ingredient named either `lettuce` or `tomato`. The","+conditions cannot be satisfied by different ingredients.","+","+An empty relationship does not match a nested `contains` query, but it does match nested","+`not_equals` and `equals` queries, just like JavaScript's `some` and `every` methods.","+"," ## Writing Queries"," "," Writing queries in Payload is simple and consistent across all APIs, with only minor differences in syntax between them."],"additions":96,"deletions":8,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/db-mongodb/src/queries/buildSearchParams.ts","lines":["@@ -1,9 +1,19 @@"," import type { QueryFilter } from 'mongoose'","-import type { FlattenedField, Operator, PathToQuery, Payload } from 'payload'","+import type {","+  FlattenedField,","+  HasManyRelationshipOperator,","+  Operator,","+  PathToQuery,","+  Payload,","+} from 'payload'"," "," import { Types } from 'mongoose'"," import { APIError, escapeRegExp, getFieldByPath, getLocalizedPaths } from 'payload'","-import { validOperatorSet } from 'payload/shared'","+import {","+  hasManyRelationshipOperatorSet,","+  isNestedRelationshipQuery,","+  validOperatorSet,","+} from 'payload/shared'"," "," import type { MongooseAdapter } from '../index.js'"," import type { OperatorMapKey } from './operatorMap.js'","@@ -96,6 +106,25 @@ export async function buildSearchParam({","   }"," ","   const [{ field, path }] = paths","+","+  if (","+    hasManyRelationshipOperatorSet.has(operator as HasManyRelationshipOperator) &&","+    paths.length === 1 &&","+    (field.type === 'relationship' || field.type === 'upload') &&","+    field.hasMany &&","+    typeof field.relationTo === 'string' &&","+    isNestedRelationshipQuery(val)","+  ) {","+    return buildHasManyRelationshipSearchParam({","+      field,","+      locale,","+      nestedWhere: val,","+      operator: operator as HasManyRelationshipOperator,","+      path,","+      payload,","+    })","+  }","+","   if (path) {","     const sanitizedQueryValue = sanitizeQueryValue({","       field,","@@ -128,12 +157,20 @@ export async function buildSearchParam({","       // Remove top collection and reverse array","       // to work backwards from top","       const pathsToQuery = paths.slice(1).reverse()","+      const parentPaths =